  "raw": " be required for all manufacturers.\n\nThe new electric car, called hydrogen cell electric vehicle (HEV), is expected to be competitive with hybrids and plug-in EVs for around 2,000 euros including tax. However, for this car to work, it will need an electric battery backup with around 200 kilometres of range as well as a hydrogen supply station that doesn't need refuelling all the time. The new gas production unit will also need to be cheap and have similar technology to the electrolysis systems in modern solar installations.\n\nThe technology for electrolysis, which splits water into oxygen and hydrogen, has come down from $4 per kilowatt-hour in the 1980s to around $0.45 today.\n\nA spokesman for Toyota said that the joint plan was only a \"starting point\", and that the automakers can achieve further price reductions by eliminating cost-inefficient elements such as high-tech battery storage.\n\nThe automakers will also need to find partners who",
